@startuml
title logGO - cmd/server Component Overview

package "logGO process" {
  component "config\n(env vars)" as Config
  component "internal/ingest\nRun(ctx, opts, manager)" as Ingest
  component "logGO.Manager\n(this instance's own log store)" as Manager
  component "internal/webui\nstatic UI page" as WebUI
  component "HTTP mux\nGET /, GET /entries, GET /healthz" as Mux
  file "logGO.log\n(JSON lines)" as LogFile
}

cloud "Remote conTogether instance" {
  component "GET /logs\n(REST backfill)" as ContogetherREST
  component "GET /ws/logs\n(WebSocket live tail)" as ContogetherWS
}

actor Browser

Config --> Ingest : BaseURL, APIKey, Source
Config --> Mux : Port

Ingest -down-> ContogetherREST : HTTP GET (X-API-Key header)
Ingest -down-> ContogetherWS : WS Dial (?api_key=)
Ingest -> Manager : WriteEntry(entry)\n(preserves original timestamp)

Manager -> LogFile : append (async write loop)
Mux -> Manager : ReadLogs(level, filter)
Mux -> WebUI : serve index.html

Browser -> Mux : GET / , GET /entries?level=&contains=

note right of Ingest
  The only relationship between the two
  projects: logGO is a network *client* of
  conTogether's already-existing log-reading
  endpoints. Neither imports the other's code.
end note

note bottom of Manager
  Same Manager, same package, this instance
  just happens to store entries collected
  from elsewhere instead of (or alongside)
  writing about itself.
end note

@enduml
